# 13. REGISTRATION DATA STORAGE

This is a frontend-first implementation.

Do not implement Supabase, Firebase, server APIs, or a real database in this version.

Use browser localStorage.

### Required behavior

- Save actual registration submissions.
- Preserve records across page reloads in the same browser.
- Load existing registrations when the application starts.
- Prevent duplicate registrations.
- Keep participant data consistent.
- Handle malformed or unavailable localStorage gracefully.

### Registration record structure

Each record should include:

- Registration ID.
- Event ID.
- Full Name.
- Normalized Email.
- Phone Number.
- University.
- Branch.
- Year of Study.
- Registration Timestamp.
- Registration Status.

### Duplicate registration logic

Use the combination of normalized email address and event ID.

One email may register for multiple different events.

The same email must not register twice for the same event.

Display a clear duplicate-registration message.

### Data integrity

Do not fabricate registration records.

Do not automatically populate the database with participants.

Do not generate fake registration counts.

The participant list must initially be empty.

All displayed statistics must come from real browser-local records.

### Future architecture

Create a clean data service layer so localStorage can later be replaced by Supabase without redesigning the UI.

